<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>Dawn and sunset, star and moonlight,</l><l>I can see in paradise,</l><l>But while here on earth His mercy</l><l>For my blindness will suffice.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>I no more would be delivered</l><l>From my thorn, but look for grace,</l><l>While within the veil His glory</l><l>Shineth brightly on my face.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>In the deep dark night, His beauty</l><l>I by faith, not sight, may trace;</l><l>He was ridiculed and hated,</l><l>Yet I see His glorious face.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>Sun and moonlight far surpassing,</l><l>Clouds and Milky Way o’erspread,</l><l>Is the glory all transcending</l><l>Shining from His thorn-crowned head.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
